  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Like it says in the title, if you have a bone chain that is both being influenced by animation of some sort and (rotation specifically in my use case, with the bones in question only being influenced by one or the other) constraints, any contacts on the bone chain being moved by animation and constraints will follow the influence of animation, but not any influence from constraints.\nIf there are no animations, at all, in any capacity, on a chain, then contacts will follow the rotation constrained chain just fine. And if you have a chain animated with animations, then it will work just as well of course. But cross the streams, and contacts ignore motion from constraints.",
